# Wave W17-X (Route 212 — South): lily post — a lily-pad marker post at the loudest pools: a weathered post with a single lily pad and its blush bud floating at its foot, marking the pools the VENOFROG owns loudest (design: VENOFROG loud on lily pads through all the reeds — the frogs are creature layer, the pads at the posts are this prop’s). On bog turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 212 — North’s reed posts by the pad entire: the North marks the last footing, the South marks the water itself.
